drm/amdgpu: Bound GPIO I2C table entry count from VBIOS

jira KERNEL-1911
cve CVE-2026-97493
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.186.1.el8_10
commit-author Candice Li <candice.li@amd.com>
commit a99cd231cd924b7160fecb9fb3a94b801522323b
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.186.1.el8_10/a99cd231.failed

Reject undersized tables and cap the derived entry count
to AMDGPU_MAX_I2C_BUS so we do not overrun adev->i2c_bus[]
or walk an absurd number of entries on corrupt size fields.

	Signed-off-by: Candice Li <candice.li@amd.com>
	Reviewed-by: Tao Zhou <tao.zhou1@amd.com>
	Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
(cherry picked from commit a99cd231cd924b7160fecb9fb3a94b801522323b)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_atombios.c
diff --cc drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_atombios.c
